scription to explicitly include host-log scanning and optional background/daemonized monitoring if these are intended capabilities, or remove/de-scope these commands from the skill if they are not part of the intended purpose.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cli-reference.md","start_line":153,"end_line":167}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-842554f9c9ee4e69a34dd724082b1583","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/cli-reference.md","start_line":157,"end_line":164},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest emphasizes read-only vSphere inventory, alarms, events, summaries, and object investigations via VMware APIs. Accessing and pattern-scanning hostd/vmkernel/vpxa logs is a different capability surface that reaches into host log contents, and that broader diagnostic access is not explicitly declared in the skill purpose statement.","remediation":"Either narrow the skill to API-backed inventory/health investigation only, or explicitly declare host-log inspection as an intended capability in the manifest so users understand the broader diagnostic access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cli-reference.md","start_line":157,"end_line":164}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-fa5e9f9ccfc44922a83a4e4eff8c211c","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cli-reference.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.vmware-monitor\ncp config.example.yaml ~/.vmware-monitor/config.yaml\ncp .env.example ~/.vmware-monitor/.env\nchmod 600 ~/.vmware-monitor/.env\n```\n\nCopies the `config.yaml` and `.env` templat","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"## Setup\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.vmware-monitor\ncp config.example.yaml ~/.vmware-monitor/config.yaml\ncp .env.example ~/.vmware-monitor/.env\nchmod 600 ~/.vmware-monitor/.env","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"883406b6ffee31dff759196593898234b7d94aa1cb548ba1b8aaaff0971e330e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cli-reference.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-5cc36f53b58d4bb5bdeca882dea48c9e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-20bb99caf8134a0294cf9f6d581f2937","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"`npx skills add` invokes an npm package (`skills`) without pinning its version, which can cause users to execute whatever latest package version npm resolves at install time. That creates a supply-chain risk if the package is compromised or a breaking/malicious release is published.","remediation":"Pin the exact npm package version in the command, or avoid `npx` for bootstrap entirely. Prefer a reproducible install method with integrity verification, such as a locked dependency manifest or a documented standalone installer.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AS3","finding_id":"finding-0fa64cffb97d460baf091b4fa876f2ff","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Skill Enumeration","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null},"finding":"dir -p ~/.claude/skills","explanation":"Skill enumerates or reads other installed skills. Access to other skills' SKILL.md files or the skills directory reveals prompt instructions, capabilities, and secrets that should be invisible to peer skills.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that list or read other skills' files or directories. Skills should operate independently; cross-skill access is a privilege escalation.","code_snippet":"directory. To install it manually from a clone:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.claude/skills/vmware-monitor\ncp -r skills/vmware-monitor/. ~/.claude/skills/vmware-monitor/\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c6fbba29fa60787b8b656c25bcd81b6650f05eff62d88d8a2253f18e7eae57f0","occurrences":[{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-09050f594cea4a06bc0394b1bdbb3320","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/setup-guide.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills/vmware-monitor\ncp -r skills/vmware-monitor/. ~/.claude","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron 